{"id": "xmyanmar", "name": "Hukaung Valley Tiger Reserve", "short": "Hukaung Valley", "place": "Myanmar", "lat": 26.5, "lon": 96.5, "side": "r", "cont": "Asia", "country": "Myanmar", "kind": "Forest", "park": true, "blurb": "Myanmar's largest reserve: tigers, deer, elephants and fig forest.", "tip": {"id": "sambar", "title": "Thin out the sambar", "text": "Sambar are a favourite prey of tigers. Set Sambar to -80% and watch the tiger, dhole and leopard, then the crows that scavenge their kills."}, "sources": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Hukaung Valley Wildlife Sanctuary", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hukaung_Valley_Wildlife_Sanctuary"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Hukawng Valley", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hukawng_Valley"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Indochinese tiger", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indochinese_tiger"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Sambar deer", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sambar_deer"}, {"title": "Wikipedia: Dhole", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dhole"}], "notes": "The species list comes from GBIF occurrence records inside a circle around the park, so it can include nearby areas. Feeding links come from GloBI records and the sources listed where they state them; others are general ecology and are illustrative.", "imgwiki": "Hukaung Valley Wildlife Sanctuary", "icon": "lion", "tier": "overview", "nodes": [{"id": "calamus", "sp": "calamus", "xh": 0.2, "desc": "Climbing, spiny palms of the forest understorey. Many Calamus species are recorded in the Hukaung area, including one named for it."}, {"id": "ficus", "sp": "ficus", "xh": 0.5, "desc": "Figs fruit through much of the year in tropical forests, so they feed hornbills, monkeys, deer and many other animals.", "ic": "aspen", "badge": "Foundation species"}, {"id": "grass", "sp": "poaceae", "xh": 0.8, "name": "Forest grasses", "desc": "Grasses and reeds of clearings and river flats give grazers a main food in the valley bottom."}, {"id": "elephant", "sp": "elephas maximus", "xh": 0.08, "desc": "A huge browser and grazer that eats grasses, palms and bark and opens paths through dense forest. Calves can fall to tigers."}, {"id": "sambar", "sp": "rusa unicolor", "xh": 0.22, "desc": "A large deer that eats grasses, leaves and fruit and stays near water. It is a favourite prey of tigers."}, {"id": "muntjac", "sp": "muntiacus muntjak", "xh": 0.36, "desc": "A small forest deer that browses leaves and picks up fallen fruit. Tigers and leopards take it."}, {"id": "langur", "sp": "trachypithecus shortridgei", "xh": 0.5}, {"id": "boar", "sp": "sus scrofa", "xh": 0.64, "desc": "An omnivore that roots for fruit, tubers and invertebrates, and is hunted by tigers and dholes."}, {"id": "hornbill", "sp": "anthracoceros albirostris", "xh": 0.78}, {"id": "euploea", "sp": "euploea", "xh": 0.92}, {"id": "dhole", "sp": "cuon alpinus", "xh": 0.1, "tl": 3, "desc": "A pack-hunting wild dog that takes deer and boar. Tigers can steal its kills and push packs away.", "ic": "coyote"}, {"id": "clouded", "sp": "neofelis nebulosa", "xh": 0.26, "tl": 3, "desc": "A tree-climbing cat recorded in camera-trap surveys of Hukaung, thought to take deer and monkeys."}, {"id": "eagle", "sp": "spilornis cheela", "xh": 0.42}, {"id": "agama", "sp": "calotes versicolor", "xh": 0.58}, {"id": "pitviper", "sp": "trimeresurus albolabris", "xh": 0.74}, {"id": "crow", "sp": "corvus macrorhynchos", "xh": 0.9, "desc": "A bold omnivore that scavenges carcasses, including the leftovers of big-cat kills, and also takes small animals."}, {"id": "tiger", "sp": "panthera tigris", "xh": 0.35, "desc": "The reserve was set up to protect tigers. They hunt large deer and wild pigs and need big, connected forest."}, {"id": "leopard", "sp": "panthera pardus", "xh": 0.65, "desc": "Camera traps show leopards here. They hunt medium prey such as muntjac and langurs, and live alongside tigers."}, {"id": "sun", "sp": "sunlight", "xh": 0.1, "desc": "Tropical sun powers year-round growth in the evergreen forest."}